WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.260
Speaker 1: One of the things that is important
to prevent, because once the cat is out of

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.680
the bag, it's very difficult to get it back
in is the rewriting of history any time that

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.680
we can.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:17.730
And when it comes to the last couple of years,
the pandemic, the Trump administration, et

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:23.300
cetera, we've been covering it all closely
with you with no interruption.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:29.330
And so it gives us sort of this perspective
where we can remember what things were like

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:37.100
last year or two years ago when the right
tries to rewrite history for political advantage

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.710
or whatever the case may be.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:45.160
Now this is a politically biased show in the
sense that this might come as a shock to some

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.180
of you, which is a problem, but this is not
a news reporting show.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.600
This is a news, commentary and analysis show.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.600
I'm on the left.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.620
I'm a progressive.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.370
That's my perspective.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:00.469
But one of the things that I always try to
do or try not to do, depending on your perspective,

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:08.749
is I don't want to toss the political football
back and forth on issues that are not really

00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:10.359
worthy of that.

00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:12.680
And you know that on debt and deficit.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.750
I don't play into the debt and deficit games
that both Republicans and Democrats play,

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.950
but Republicans play it more for sure because
they're the ones who claim to be the party

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:26.259
of fiscal responsibility as they define it
on gas prices, for example.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:30.240
I've told you guys this, and when it was Bush
that was president, when it was Obama, when

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.240
it was Trump.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.950
Now under Joe Biden, the American president
has very little influence over gas prices,

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:42.889
so I don't use gas prices as something to
praise or beat down a president.

00:01:42.889 --> 00:01:44.130
These games are boring to me.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.679
We're beyond them.

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:54.159
And now the issue of supply chain and shortages
is taking exactly the same tone and color.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:55.569
It's Joe Biden's fault.

00:01:55.569 --> 00:02:00.099
If as the other day when I went to the grocery
store, I couldn't get my Granny Smith apples

00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:03.509
and I tweeted about it and got into a funny
exchange with Sam Seder about it.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:06.069
But I'm not blaming Joe Biden for that.

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:10.239
Much like I didn't blame Donald Trump for
the shortages we saw earlier in the pandemic.

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:16.099
But the right wants to play the games, and
Tom not only is the right now blaming Joe

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:20.959
Biden for everything that's going on and saying,
Well, we have shortages because Secretary

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:25.950
of Transportation Pete Boudette, judge was
on paternity leave.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.890
It even led to sort of homophobic stuff about,
Oh, he's learning to breastfeed and stuff

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.970
like this.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:34.709
And now Republican Senator Tom Cotton.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:40.459
Tom Cotton went on Laura Ingraham Show last
night and said we didn't have shortages under

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.700
Donald Trump during the first year of the
pandemic.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.909
What this is beyond parody.

00:02:46.909 --> 00:02:47.939
Take a listen to this.

00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:52.170
Speaker 2: Early in the morning, you know,
we've had this pandemic for two years, Laura.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.510
I don't remember inflation or supply chain
shortages or labor shortages that we've seen

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.370
this year in the first year of the pandemic.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.370
What changed?

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.859
Joe Biden and the Democrats took power in
January.

00:03:01.859 --> 00:03:03.989
Speaker 1: Can you imagine?

00:03:03.989 --> 00:03:07.090
Can you imagine so labor shortages?

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.600
Well, that's very, very silly.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:20.249
During the vast majority of Trump's presidency
during the pandemic, things were shut down.

00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:25.959
There were too many workers in the sense that
a ton of businesses were closed.

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:32.959
Entertainment venues, movie theaters, sporting
events, many restaurants when it came to in-house

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:35.450
dining rather than just take out.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.519
The situation was completely different.

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:40.739
That's why there weren't so-called labor shortages
under Trump.

00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:44.670
Now, whether they are even really shortages
now, I think that that's actually the wrong

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.670
term for them.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.450
But that's very silly.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.639
But he's saying there were supply chain issues.

00:03:49.639 --> 00:03:52.379
Do you guys remember toilet paper under Donald
Trump?

00:03:52.379 --> 00:03:55.280
You couldn't find toilet paper when it came
back in stock.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.420
There were limits.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.249
No one package per person.

00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:01.529
You can't get two packages of toilet paper
under Trump.

00:04:01.529 --> 00:04:02.799
Was I blaming Trump for that?

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:03.799
Of course not.

00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:05.060
It had nothing to do with Trump.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.579
There were no N95 masks available.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:10.060
There were no N95 masks available.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.489
People were desperate to get those surgical
masks.

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:14.560
You couldn't get hand sanitizer.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.049
Couldn't find sanitizing wipes on Amazon.

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:18.680
Your local CVS couldn't find it.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:24.120
The Lysol and other sprays, I wanted to get
rubbing alcohol sold out everywhere.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.930
I ended up ordering a two pack from like target
online or something like that.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.120
There were no canned foods you'd go to the
grocery store.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:36.170
Not only was the grocery store packed with
lines waiting outside.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.870
You couldn't find canned soup.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.000
You couldn't find black beans.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.160
You couldn't find pinto beans.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.380
You couldn't find kidney beans, you couldn't
find cannellini beans, you couldn't find refried

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.380
beans.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.380
You couldn't find spicy refried beans.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.920
You couldn't find fava beans.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.920
OK, I could go on.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.920
I'm big on beans.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.810
As you can tell the dry pasta section empty.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.639
No spaghetti, no ziti, no penny, no gnocchi,
no pepper deli, no rotini.

00:04:56.639 --> 00:04:58.450
Linguine angel hair.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:03.660
Atopy, tagliatelle, fusilli macaroni farfalle
Consiglio.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:07.771
You couldn't find lasagna noodles, guys, lasagna
noodles I was trying to make lasagna, couldn't

00:05:07.771 --> 00:05:09.259
find them.

00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:12.449
Costco was limiting how much meat you could
buy.

00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:16.650
Meat was being rationed, folks, Whole Foods
said.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.490
Only one of each kind of frozen fruit or vegetable.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.960
I wanted to packages a frozen mango.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.310
I was only allowed to buy one.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.690
There was no flour and sugar.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.600
People were baking like crazy due to boredom.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.530
Couldn't dub ammunition was sold out everywhere.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:33.560
Remember that?

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:42.639
And Tom Cotton doesn't remember anything like
this before this year under Joe Biden.

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:43.669
What?

00:05:43.669 --> 00:05:48.660
But the important thing is, no one was blaming
Trump for that back then.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:53.319
Even people on the left weren't saying It's
Trump's fault that there is no toilet paper

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:58.139
because it would be idiotic, just like the
other day at the grocery store.

00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:02.810
I wanted my beloved Granny Smith apples and
they were sold out.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:04.250
Thanksgiving probably had something to do
with it.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.250
The green apple.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.240
Very, very strong for Apple Pie.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.979
Let's put that aside, it's not just but Joe
Biden's fault.

00:06:10.979 --> 00:06:13.430
If anything, it's Thanksgiving's fault.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.430
OK?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.430
These guys have to give it up.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:20.590
I mean, we it's on us not to allow them to
get away with this.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:26.490
It was not Trump's fault, but there were shortages
under Trump, and it is not Joe Biden's fault

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:31.790
that now, you know, I wanted to get quiche
crusts the other day and they were sold out.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:36.949
I'm not blaming Pete Boudette judges premature
twins that he has adopted.

00:06:36.949 --> 00:06:38.430
It's just it just has nothing to do with that.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.430
It's very silly.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:07:40.899
Let's not allow them to rewrite history.

